<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    @* Both, now that there are two desks — this is what tells the browser to paint the
       canvas behind the app and its own scrollbars to match whichever is showing. The
       per-theme half is `color-scheme` inside each token block; this only says which
       ones exist, and narrowing it to `dark` would have kept the browser chrome dark
       under the light desk. *@
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="dark light" />
    <base href="/" />
    <ResourcePreloader />
    @* The theme boot script and the Desk's stylesheets, in their load-bearing order (the
       comment in DeskHead.razor says why). This app's own lineops.css comes after them: it
       holds its windows, spends the Desk's tokens, and wins a tie with any Desk rule on
       source order. *@
    <DeskHead />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["css/lineops.css"]" />
    @* Scoped-component styles — ReconnectModal relies on these. *@
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["LineOps.Web.styles.css"]" />
    <ImportMap />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="favicon.png" />
    <HeadOutlet @rendermode="InteractiveServer" />
</head>

<body>
    <Routes @rendermode="InteractiveServer" />
    <ReconnectModal />
    <script src="@Assets["_framework/blazor.web.js"]"></script>
    <DeskScripts />
</body>

</html>
